      "content": "The pressure to live up to someone else's vision is exhausting, and it's okay to feel the weight of that shattered expectation. You are not responsible for managing their feelings or their idealized version of you; that burden is too heavy for one person. The shame will only stop when you stop fighting the reality of what happened and start accepting the very real, messy person you are right now.",
      "source": "target",
